{
 "_comment": "Per-fw gadget + kernel-offset table for lapse. Two ROP bases: `webkit` = libSceNKWebKit.sprx (slopkit.webkitBase). `libkernel_web` = libkernel_web.sprx (slopkit.kernelBase). All gadgets pad=0 (clean pop; ret) so lapse.js's chain-building convention works without modification. mov_rax_0x200000000 does not exist in either module \u2014 lapse.js patched to use pop_rax + 0x200000000n. GENERATED by offsets/extract-gadgets.py \u2014 do not hand-edit. Covers 09.00 \u2192 12.00, the full netcontrol-UAF window. Every RVA is the first occurrence of the gadget's byte pattern in the module's executable PT_LOAD, and each one was disassembled and string-matched against its `desc` before being written. setjmp/longjmp are recovered by prologue signature (the original 0x58f80/0x58fd0 pointed at data). `ret` was 0xc2 on every firmware, which actually decodes to `pop r14; pop r15; pop rbp; ret`; it is now a true one-byte ret \u2014 nothing reads ROP.ret today, so that is a latent-bug fix rather than a behaviour change.",
